# agent-id-enum-lint baseline (IMP-036 SCOPE-7)
#
# Pre-existing free-text agent ids observed across the six consuming repos on
# 2026-08-06. They are frozen here so the lint can run at all; hard-failing
# thousands of historical records would make it unrunnable and therefore
# ignored.
#
# This file may only SHRINK. Never add an id here to silence a failure - that
# inverts the ratchet and turns the lint into decoration. A genuinely new agent
# is added to bubbles/agent-capabilities.yaml instead.
#
# Regenerate deliberately (single repo):
#   bash bubbles/scripts/agent-id-enum-lint.sh <repo> --update-baseline
#
# The categories below are the migration map. Each has a different remedy.

# --- retired agents that no longer ship ---------------------------------------
# Remedy: nothing to do. These disappear as their specs age out.
bubbles.analyze
bubbles.bootstrap
bubbles.certify
bubbles.discovery
bubbles.finalize
bubbles.governance-remediation
bubbles.improve
bubbles.plan-legacy-discharge
bubbles.planning
bubbles.reconcile
bubbles.release
bubbles.select
bubbles.shepherd
bubbles.spec

# --- legacy ralph.* family (pre-bubbles naming) -------------------------------
# Remedy: nothing to do. Historical only; no ralph.* agent ships today.
ralph.analyst
ralph.analyst + ralph.ux
ralph.audit
ralph.chaos
ralph.design
ralph.docs
ralph.gaps
ralph.harden
ralph.implement
ralph.iterate
ralph.plan
ralph.security
ralph.stabilize
ralph.test
ralph.ux
ralph.validate
ralph.workflow

# --- composite ids: several agents recorded in ONE field ----------------------
# Remedy: one executionHistory entry per agent. A composite id is the clearest
# case of the field carrying data the schema has no place for.
bubbles.analyst+ux+design+plan
bubbles.design+bubbles.plan
bubbles.gaps+plan
bubbles.goal/bubbles.bug
bubbles.implement+test+validate+audit+docs
bubbles.improve+plan
bubbles.workflow gaps-to-doc
bubbles.workflow/security-to-doc

# --- scope suffix welded onto the agent id ------------------------------------
# Remedy: the scope belongs in the entry's own scope field, not the agent id.
bubbles.implement-scope-01
bubbles.implement-scope-02
bubbles.implement-scope-03
bubbles.implement-scope-04
bubbles.implement-scope-05

# --- non-agent actors and sweep pseudo-agents ---------------------------------
# Remedy: use one of the NON_AGENT_ACTORS values (manual, operator, human), or
# record the sweep in a sibling field with the real agent in `agent`.
ADOPT-EXISTING
GitHub Copilot
controller
github-copilot
orchestrator
pre-push gate
stochastic-quality-sweep
system-review-2026-03-25
system-sweep
